- Reader's timeline: every journal of one feed merged into a single
- chronological strip, freshest first. Drafts never show up here.
-
- Everything that navigates is a real $mol_link, so the rendered html carries an
- <a href> a crawler can follow. A click handler on a $mol_view would move the
- reader just fine and leave the post unindexed.
$bog_journal_feed_page $mol_view
	feed_link \
	title_fallback @ \Feed
	subscribe_hint @ \Journal link
	subscribe_add @ \Follow
	subscribe_bad @ \That does not look like a journal link.
	subscribe_dup @ \This journal is already in the feed.
	source_wait @ \loading
	source_fail @ \unavailable
	empty_none @ \No journals yet. Paste a link to one above and its posts will show up here.
	empty_quiet @ \Nothing published yet.
	empty_nofeed @ \No feed opened.
	author_unnamed @ \Unnamed author
	post_untitled @ \Untitled post
	sub /
		<= Head $mol_view
			sub <= head_content /
				<= Title $mol_paragraph
					title <= title_shown \
				<= Subscribe $mol_view
					sub /
						<= Subscribe_input $mol_string
							hint <= subscribe_hint
							value? <=> subscribe_draft? \
							submit?event <=> subscribe?event null
						<= Subscribe_button $mol_button_major
							title <= subscribe_add
							click?event <=> subscribe?event null
				<= Subscribe_error $mol_paragraph
					title <= subscribe_error? \
		<= Sources $mol_view
			sub <= source_rows /
		<= Posts $mol_view
			sub <= card_rows /
		<= Empty $mol_paragraph
			title <= empty_text \
	Source* $bog_journal_feed_source
		author_arg <= source_arg* *
		title <= source_name* \
		status <= source_status* \
		drop?event <=> source_drop*?event null
	Card* $bog_journal_feed_card
		post_arg <= post_arg* *
		author_arg <= author_arg* *
		title <= post_title* \
		summary <= post_summary* \
		author_name <= post_author_name* \
		avatar_file <= post_avatar_file* \
		avatar_seed <= post_author* \
		moment <= post_moment* \
		cover_uri <= post_cover_uri* \
		has_cover <= post_has_cover* false
		tags <= post_tags* /

- One post in the timeline. Cover, title and author are three separate anchors
- rather than one card-sized link: an <a> nested in an <a> is invalid html and
- the parser tears such markup apart.
$bog_journal_feed_card $mol_view
	dom_name \article
	post_arg *
	author_arg *
	title \
	summary \
	author_name \
	avatar_file \
	avatar_seed \
	moment \
	cover_uri \
	has_cover false
	tags /
	sub <= card_content /
		<= Cover_link $mol_link
			arg <= post_arg
			hint <= title
			sub /
				<= Cover $mol_image
					uri <= cover_uri
					title <= title
		<= Body $mol_view
			sub /
				<= Title_link $mol_link
					arg <= post_arg
					title <= title
				<= Summary $mol_paragraph
					title <= summary
				<= Tags $mol_view
					sub <= tag_rows /
				<= Foot $mol_view
					sub /
						<= Author_link $mol_link
							arg <= author_arg
							hint <= author_name
							sub /
								<= Avatar $bog_journal_feed_avatar
									file_link <= avatar_file
									seed <= avatar_seed
									hint <= author_name
								<= Author_name $mol_paragraph
									title <= author_name
						<= Moment $mol_paragraph
							title <= moment
	Tag* $mol_view
		sub /
			<= tag_text* \

- Author's picture. A view of its own so a cover-sized blob still loading
- suspends just this circle instead of the card around it.
$bog_journal_feed_avatar $mol_view
	file_link \
	seed \
	hint \
	sub <= face /
	Picture $mol_image
		uri <= uri \
		title <= hint
	Fallback $mol_avatar
		id <= seed

- One subscription: where it leads, whether it arrived, and a way out of it.
$bog_journal_feed_source $mol_view
	author_arg *
	title \
	status \
	drop?event null
	sub /
		<= Open $mol_link
			arg <= author_arg
			title <= title
		<= Status $mol_paragraph
			title <= status
		<= Drop $mol_button_minor
			hint @ \Unfollow
			click?event <=> drop?event null
			sub /
				<= Drop_icon $mol_icon_close
